# Issue #278 proof corpus — SELECTOR-REGEX MATCHER SEMANTICS.
#
# The promqltest store stands in for the ClickHouse fetch layer, and until
# this file existed its matcher compiled `regex::Regex::new(&format!(
# "^(?:{pattern})$"))` — a second, private implementation of matcher
# semantics that disagreed with Prometheus AND with our own production
# engine, which compiles `pulsus_re2::compile_user_regex_anchored(
# &pulsus_re2::re2_pattern_to_rust(p))` (crates/pulsus-read/src/metrics/
# labels.rs:274 and :620). The harness was therefore LESS correct than the
# code it validates: it would have rejected a Prometheus-captured
# expectation and green-lit a wrong one.
#
# Every eval row below is a bare vector selector carrying exactly ONE
# non-__name__ regex matcher, so `plan()` files it under
# `SelectorSpec::matchers` and the store's matcher loop is the only thing
# that can exclude a series — no aggregation, no function, no __name__
# regex, nothing that could make an answer come out right for another
# reason.
#
# PROVENANCE OF THE EXPECTATIONS. Captured from `prom/prometheus:v3.13.0`,
# image digest
#   sha256:0e698e35e50d1ddc2d11a4a55b089fe62eb71358a5c204dfafd21bdf8ffe04b8
# which self-reports at /api/v1/status/buildinfo: version 3.13.0, revision
# 40af9c2cdc0eda00f3622e867a27f6359f7295f3 — the same commit
# corpus/upstream-manifest.json pins (`prometheus_sha`). Capture route: the
# fixture below was served as a static text-exposition endpoint, scraped by
# that container, and the answers read back through GET /api/v1/query.
# Captured 2026-08-24.
#
# WHY THESE VALUES. Each is a fragment-level trap for one Perl class as the
# Rust `regex` crate reads it and RE2 does not:
#
#   U+00B5 MICRO SIGN          Unicode \w, NOT ASCII \w
#   U+0663 ARABIC-INDIC THREE  Unicode \d, NOT ASCII \d
#   U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE      Unicode \s, NOT RE2 \s (which is [\t\n\f\r ])
#   a{,3}                      RE2 reads the literal text `a{,3}`; the Rust
#                              crate rejects the pattern outright, which
#                              aborted the WHOLE file, not just one row
#
# RE2's ASCII class definitions: re2/parse.cc kPerlDigit/kPerlSpace/
# kPerlWord, mirrored in crates/pulsus-re2/src/re2_syntax.rs.
#
# A ninth reference value, `a<U+000B>b` (VERTICAL TAB — Unicode \s but not
# RE2 \s), is deliberately absent: an invisible control byte makes an
# unreviewable diff. It is a Rust unit test instead,
# promqltest/store.rs::tests::a_vertical_tab_is_not_re2_whitespace. The
# reference capture carried it, so the `!~` row's answer is seven series
# there and the six below here.

load 1m
	p278{lbl="aµb"}	1
	p278{lbl="a٣b"}	2
	p278{lbl="a b"}	3
	p278{lbl="ab"}	5
	p278{lbl="a{,3}"}	6
	p278{lbl="awb"}	7
	p278{lbl="a3b"}	8
	p278{lbl="a b"}	9

# ASCII \w only: the letter `w` and the digit `3` match; U+00B5 and
# U+0663 do not, though both are Unicode \w.
eval instant at 0 p278{lbl=~"a\\wb"}
	p278{lbl="awb"} 7
	p278{lbl="a3b"} 8

# ASCII \d only: U+0663 ARABIC-INDIC DIGIT THREE is a Unicode digit
# and must NOT match.
eval instant at 0 p278{lbl=~"a\\db"}
	p278{lbl="a3b"} 8

# RE2 \s is [\t\n\f\r ] — five characters. U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE is
# Unicode whitespace and must NOT match; only the U+0020 series does.
eval instant at 0 p278{lbl=~"a\\sb"}
	p278{lbl="a b"} 9

# `{,3}` is not a well-formed repetition, so RE2 takes it as the
# literal text `a{,3}`. Under the old matcher this row did not merely
# fail — `Regex::new` returned Err, the driver's fetch errored and the
# whole file aborted.
eval instant at 0 p278{lbl=~"a{,3}"}
	p278{lbl="a{,3}"} 6

# The negation, so an over-matching \w is caught from the other side
# too: a matcher that wrongly INCLUDED U+00B5/U+0663 above would
# wrongly EXCLUDE them here.
eval instant at 0 p278{lbl!~"a\\wb"}
	p278{lbl="aµb"} 1
	p278{lbl="a٣b"} 2
	p278{lbl="a b"} 3
	p278{lbl="ab"} 5
	p278{lbl="a{,3}"} 6
	p278{lbl="a b"} 9
